course: dictionary
lesson: 15323
title: Snarl: growls, angry voices and tangles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Snarl is a word with a few related meanings, so context tells you which one is right. When an animal snarls, it shows its teeth and makes a deep, angry growl. «The dog began to snarl at the postman.» The word snarl is the warning sign here.
explain: When a person snarls, they speak in an angry, nasty voice. «"Get out of my room!" she snarled.» She is not growling like a dog. The angry, nasty voice is the clue, so snarled means she said it in a cross way.
explain: A snarl can also be a tangle, like a knot in hair, string or wool. «My hair had a snarl at the back after the windy walk.» The word snarl can also be a noun, like «a snarl of wires». Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence: an angry growl, or a knot?
fact: Snarl is a verb (snarl, snarls, snarled, snarling) and a noun (a snarl, snarls).
fact: «Snarl» means to show your teeth and make a deep, angry growl, as a dog does.
fact: When a person snarls, they say something in an angry, nasty voice.
fact: A snarl can be a tangle, a knot of hair, string or wool.
fact: «Snarl-up» (UK) means a traffic jam, where cars get stuck and tangled up.
exercise: «The dog began to snarl at the postman, showing its sharp teeth.» What does snarl mean here? | *An angry growl with teeth showing | Wagging its tail happily | Barking a happy song | Sleeping by the front door
exercise: «"Get out of my room!" she snarled.» How does she speak? | In a soft, sleepy voice | In a whisper to a friend | *In an angry, nasty voice | In a happy, singing voice
exercise: «The rain caused a snarl-up on the motorway, and cars were stuck for hours.» What is a snarl-up? | A new road sign | A fast race between cars | A type of car engine | *A traffic jam
test: «My little brother's hair had a big snarl at the back.» What is a snarl here? | A happy smile | A long holiday | A loud animal sound | *A knot or tangle
test: «Be careful: a wolf that snarls is warning you to back away.» What does the snarl warn you about? | That the wolf wants to play | *That the wolf is angry and may attack | That the wolf is sleepy | That the wolf is lost
exam: «The wires behind the TV were a snarl, so Dad could not find which one to plug in.» What does a snarl of wires mean? | A kind of TV show | A small, bright light | *A tangled knot of wires | Wires that are brand new
